  "gaps": [
    "CRIT 100 is listed both as a Professional (Required) course and as the General Education 'Integration' requirement; the capture does not say whether one 3-credit course satisfies both. It is listed once above, so the ledger sums to 57 credits against the stated split of Professional 18 + General Education 21 + General Electives 21 = 60. The remaining 3 credits are unaccounted for.",
    "Catalog year/term is not stated; only tuition for 'Fall '26 - Summer '27' and start dates are given.",
    "Residency requirement is implied but not tied to specific courses. The capture states 'CCO accepts up to 45 transfer credits toward an associate degree' but does not say which courses must be taken at Champlain.",
    "The capture does not say whether the 6 credits of 100/200-level professional courses may overlap with General Education selections.",
    "The Program Curriculum section refers to 'online business management courses', which appears to be inconsistent boilerplate for a General Studies program.",
    "Minimum grade and GPA requirements for graduation are not stated.",
    "The Arts, Humanities, and Social Science option list includes MGMT 365, a 300-level course. Course-level restrictions for General Education are not clarified."
  ],
